{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496126-can-anyone-explain-the-paradigms-of-the-mage-factions-for-me","id":1496126,"title":"Can anyone explain the paradigms of the Mage factions for me?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-02T14:20:29-07:00","id":1496126,"title":"Can anyone explain the paradigms of the Mage factions for me?","content":"I am kinda confused by them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27644-thecursedkatana","name":"Thecursedkatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:08:41-07:00","id":1496130,"title":"","content":"The major factions don't really have single paradigms to explain. They exist as an overarching philosophic structure to allow mages of differing paradigms to communicate and cooperate with each other to a common goal. <br /> <br /> For example, the Council of Nine Traditions exists in modern times primarily to promote a pluralistic concept of magic where all paradigms are equally valid, and thus are strongly opposed to the Technocratic Union - who want to select a subset of paradigms to be privileged over others - and the more destructive nature of the Nephandi and Marauders, while only weakly opposed to the Disparate Alliance who want magical practices to be left to their own devices rather than enter into the Traditions' desire for a unified vision.<br /> <br /> Even each individual Tradition/Convention/Craft within those groups have internal diversity. Paradigm is ultimately an individual belief structure informed by learning from other people. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:23:37-07:00","id":1496131,"title":"","content":"Order of hermes paradigm, what is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27644-thecursedkatana","name":"Thecursedkatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:36:54-07:00","id":1496132,"title":"","content":"Like I said, there isn't one. The Order of Hermes has a philosophy around how to get mages of different teaching lineages to unite under one banner, but many paradigms coexist under the Order's umbrella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:50:08-07:00","id":1496135,"title":"","content":"I understand, what exactly is that philosophy, and how do they teach magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27644-thecursedkatana","name":"Thecursedkatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T16:20:05-07:00","id":1496136,"title":"","content":"The Order's philosophy is based in two essential concepts. First is a proto-science (think the classical Greek philosophers that laid the foundations for what would become modern science later) approach to magic where they seek to identify fundamental concepts all magic uses, so they can classify it and create a mutual &quot;language&quot; around what people are doing. Many of the game terms that exist in-universe ones as well, come from the Order because they came in with a broad set of terminology so mages from all over Europe and the Mediterranean could discuss theory together even while they differed in process.<br /> <br /> Second, the Order heavily believes that magic is an act of individual will. Individual Hemetics might refer to this as fortitude, dominance, control, precision or whatever, the key of what unites these teachings is that they're ultimately about providing structure for a mage to exert their will on the world via magical practice.<br /> <br /> These directly inform their teaching methods. The Order prefers highly systemic and academic education where their initiates study magical theory in great depth. They focus instruction on how exact execution of magical principles produces desired results, because that dedication is the foundation on which they built their individual will and then grow as mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T18:02:52-07:00","id":1496144,"title":"","content":"I recommend watching the <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Sdb_gIF8JVE\" target=\"_blank\"> Mage:The Podcast</a> episide on their Tradition book. It explains the paradigm concisely, provides some evocative quotes and excellent plot hooks. They have an episode for each Tradition and Convention, its the easiest way to get a solid understanding of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T10:22:25-08:00","id":1496317,"title":"","content":"Reading the main / overall MtA books would be a good start in regard to beliefs, methods, approaches, Paradigms, and philosophies of various particular Mages and the different Mage groups and organizations. The various Corebooks and also the Storyteller's Companion are definitely good enough. I would also certianly recommend the Book of Shadows and the Book of Chantries. I would like to note that it is very important to carefully consider and connect the infomration and facts from the different chapters, no matter how varied or unrelated they might seem at first.<br /> <br /> The pictures and illustrations in these books are very interesting and complex.It is certainly worth it to analyze and consider them carefully and extensively while reading through the paragraphs of these MtA books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T02:27:01-08:00","id":1502681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thecursedkatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496126-can-anyone-explain-the-paradigms-of-the-mage-factions-for-me?p=1496131#post1496131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order of hermes paradigm, what is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you already ask this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}